      "body": "AUTHOR: Grifter\nTOOL: Grifter's Gift\nUSE: Stealing cargo ships\n\nWorking notes: Grifter's Gift / Cargo Transfer Protocol.\n\nCore trick:\nThe box spoofs cargo authority, not command authority. Haulers trust cargo instructions because haulers are built by people who think moving boxes quickly is more important than asking why the boxes are moving. Push the right handshake through Relay and the hauler starts acting like it belongs to the ship sending it.\n\nField use:\n\n1. Pick a hauler. Flag does not matter. Ghost, Umbra, TSN, UFN, same weak little cargo spine.\n2. Get close. Inside 2.0u is where the link bites.\n3. Relay should show Cargo Transfer Protocol once the box sees a valid hauler.\n4. Start the transfer and hold the link steady.\n5. If range breaks, the handover stalls. Get close again and let it keep chewing.\n6. Once the handover completes, the hauler should accept the operator's faction as owner.\n\nDo not waste time on fighters, guards, stations, or anything pretending it has a real command brain. Haulers only. Bigger haulers may take longer. Dead haulers transfer nothing except blame.\n\nUmbra have confirmed it works aboard their ships to convert ITG, UFN, and TSN cargo ships. Testing to be carried out on CUF ships. Payment is still due for this - I must remember to speak to Jones about that!\n\nUse the box, take the haulers, get a beer!\n\n- Grifter"
