      "group": "-- Marlow Information --",
      "body": "UFN PERSONNEL DOSSIER\n\nCLASSIFICATION: UFN Internal\nSOURCE: UFN Personnel Archive\nNAME: Commander Nathan Marlow\nSERVICE NUMBER: UFN-44781-CM\nSTATUS: Active\nCLEARANCE: Level 4\nCURRENT RECORD LOCATION: UFN Bastion Station\n\nSERVICE OVERVIEW:\n\nCommander Marlow has served with distinction across multiple assignments within the United Federation Navy. Personnel evaluations consistently identify strong leadership, sound judgement under pressure, and an excellent record of operational success.\n\nMarlow is regarded as a disciplined command officer with extensive experience in convoy protection, station liaison duties, and crisis-response coordination. His command record indicates a preference for structured planning, clear delegation, and maintaining crew cohesion during extended operations.\n\nASSIGNMENT HISTORY:\n\nRecent service records indicate four years aboard UFN Pathfinder prior to reassignment to duties at UFN Bastion Station.\n\nPrevious assignments include escort operations along contested trade routes, defensive patrols near UFN-aligned civilian corridors, and temporary command liaison postings during regional instability events.\n\nPerformance summaries from UFN Pathfinder describe Marlow as reliable under operational stress and effective when coordinating between military and civilian assets.\n\nCOMMENDATIONS:\n\nCommander Marlow has received commendations for convoy protection, crisis management, and officer development. Several reviews note a willingness to mentor junior officers beyond the requirements of his role.\n\nCommand staff have also cited Marlow for maintaining operational discipline during prolonged deployments and for preserving civilian confidence during high-risk escort assignments.\n\nMEDICAL AND PSYCHOLOGICAL STATUS:\n\nPsychological and medical evaluations remain within acceptable operational parameters.\n\nNo current restrictions are listed against active command duty. Routine evaluations recommend continued deployment eligibility, subject to standard UFN review cycles.\n\nADMINISTRATIVE NOTES:\n\nPersonnel records, archived mission reports, and assignment history are currently maintained at UFN Bastion Station.\n\nCross-reference files indicate additional operational material may be available through Bastion mission archives and station access records.\n\nEND OF FILE"
