      "group": "-- Marlow Information --",
      "body": "UFN AFTER ACTION REPORT\n\nCLASSIFICATION: Archived Mission Report\nFILE REF: AAR-77-419\nSOURCE: UFN Bastion Station\nAUTHOR: Commander Nathan Marlow\nLOCATION: Delta Corridor\nSTATUS: Archived\nARCHIVE LOCATION: UFN Bastion Station\n\nMISSION OBJECTIVE:\n\nEscort civilian relief convoy through contested territory and ensure safe arrival at UFN Bastion Station.\n\nThe convoy consisted of medical supplies, replacement atmospheric processors, water purification components, and emergency ration stores intended for distribution through UFN-aligned civilian settlements.\n\nOPERATION SUMMARY:\n\nObjective achieved.\n\nThe convoy departed under reduced visibility conditions following reports of pirate activity along the Delta Corridor. Escort vessels maintained defensive formation throughout transit and performed regular sensor sweeps ahead of the convoy route.\n\nMultiple pirate contacts were detected during the second and third legs of the journey. Intercept attempts were disrupted by coordinated escort maneuvers and controlled course adjustments ordered by Commander Marlow.\n\nThe convoy arrived safely despite repeated pirate harassment during transit. No civilian casualties were reported. Minor damage was sustained to escort vessels.\n\nCOMMAND ASSESSMENT:\n\nCommander Marlow demonstrated effective tactical leadership and maintained formation integrity throughout the operation.\n\nHis command decisions prioritized civilian survival, convoy cohesion, and controlled escalation. Records indicate he avoided unnecessary pursuit actions when hostile vessels attempted to draw escort ships away from the relief convoy.\n\nBridge logs show repeated emphasis on maintaining defensive coverage rather than seeking decisive engagement.\n\nPOST-MISSION DEBRIEF:\n\nDebrief conducted at UFN Bastion Station with support from Senior Logistics Officer Sarah Vance.\n\nOfficer Vance coordinated emergency resupply efforts, convoy intake processing, and logistics planning throughout the operation.\n\nSeveral follow-up recommendations were filed regarding convoy staging procedures, emergency cargo manifests, and relief-route scheduling.\n\nCURRENT PERSONNEL RECORD:\n\nSenior Logistics Officer Sarah Vance\nCurrent Assignment: UFN Horizon Outpost\nSector 7\n\nARCHIVE NOTE:\n\nReport archived at UFN Bastion Station.\n\nRelated materials may include station access records, logistics logs, and convoy debrief attachments held under Bastion local authority.\n\nEND OF REPORT"
