      "group": "HISTORIC LOGS",
      "body": "SOURCE: UFN after-action archive, filed 2231\nFiled: 2231\nFinal Status: TWIN PINES SECURE\n\nBATTLE FOR TWIN PINES\nAFTER-ACTION REPORT\n\nFiled: 2231\nLocation: Twin Pines\nOperation Status: COMPLETE\nStation Status: OPERATIONAL\nClassification: UFN INTERNAL\n\nUmbra forces entered the Twin Pines region in strength and initiated a coordinated assault against the station and surrounding UFN positions.\n\nFleet Command assessed the attack as an attempt to seize Twin Pines and establish permanent Umbra control within the outer sector. Given the station's importance to communications, fleet coordination, repair, resupply and logistics, substantial UFN reinforcements were committed.\n\nUFN forces established overwhelming numerical and tactical superiority shortly after reinforcement arrival. Umbra vessels made repeated attempts to penetrate the defensive perimeter but failed to significantly compromise the station.\n\nTwin Pines remained operational throughout the engagement, allowing continued coordination and support of UFN vessels.\n\nFollowing sustained losses, remaining Umbra forces withdrew.\n\nDamage to Twin Pines is assessed as moderate. Repairs are underway and no significant interruption to wider regional operations is anticipated.\n\nASSESSMENT:\nUmbra attempt to establish control of Twin Pines defeated.\n\nFINAL STATUS:\nTWIN PINES SECURE"
