      "group": "CURRENT LOGS - ALTERED 2247",
      "body": "SOURCE: UFN after-action archive, filed 2231\nFiled: 2231\nFinal Status: TWIN PINES LOST\n\nBATTLE FOR TWIN PINES\nAFTER-ACTION REPORT\n\nFiled: 2231\nLocation: Twin Pines\nOperation Status: FAILED\nStation Status: DESTROYED\nClassification: UFN INTERNAL\n\nUmbra forces entered the Twin Pines region in strength and initiated a coordinated assault against the station and surrounding UFN positions.\n\nFleet Command committed substantial reinforcements. Initial engagements strongly favoured UFN forces, which maintained numerical superiority over the attacking Umbra formation.\n\nDuring the engagement, Twin Pines reported an unauthorised intrusion into its command network.\n\nThe source could not be identified.\n\nWithin minutes, station shields were disabled, defensive weapons became unresponsive and communications with supporting UFN vessels were severely disrupted. Engineering teams were unable to regain control.\n\nAn unidentified vessel was detected operating within the engagement area immediately prior to the systems failure.\n\nThe vessel identified itself as:\n\nAXIS\n\nNo corresponding organisation, faction, vessel class or registry could be found.\n\nWith Twin Pines unable to defend itself or coordinate supporting forces, Umbra vessels penetrated the defensive perimeter.\n\nTwin Pines was subsequently destroyed.\n\nSurviving UFN vessels were ordered to withdraw pending assessment of the Fleet's ability to maintain outer-sector operations without the station's communications, repair and resupply infrastructure.\n\nASSESSMENT:\nEvidence indicates deliberate external interference. The identity, origin and objective of AXIS remain unknown.\n\nFINAL STATUS:\nTWIN PINES LOST"
